You'll spend most of your time in Patient Triage related tasks:

• Conduct a comprehensive physiotherapy assessment and safety screenings, identifying clinical red flags to determine program appropriateness.

• Clearly articulate the value and structure of the program to prospective patients, converting assessments into active participation.

• Utilize strong interpersonal communication and motivational interviewing skills to inspire patient commitment and long-term compliance.

What you need to have

• Must have a Bachelor’s degree in Physiotherapy;

• A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience in the treatment of musculoskeletal disorders AND/OR in the treatment of pelvic health disorders;

• A passion for personalized care that recognizes the whole person, and views good health as more than just the absence of disease;

• Excellent interpersonal skills that come across even through a digital care workspace, translating in the ability to engage our members;

• Hard-working and able to handle the pressure of a fast-paced environment;

• A strong commitment to data security and privacy;

• Comfortable with high-volume, repetitive assessment work;

• Fluency in English;

• Reliable internet connection and a desktop or laptop computer;

• Comfortable with web-based tools (full training provided).

A plus if you have experience in:

• Completion of additional formal pelvic health education course(s), such as level 1 pelvic coursework (or equivalent);

*The range below reflects base, variable, and equity for this role.

